{"data": [{"id": "2122133977414988192", "author_id": "1490950408272896085", "text": "@emollick Switching views in 3D without loading a new scene is a nice touch.", "created_at": "2026-11-16T01:05:42.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/daveylan2/status/2122133977414988192", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122131435070927206", "author_id": "2116149910223347712", "text": "@emollick The \"let me switch views\" bit is what gets me. A year ago that one clause was a week of camera rigging. Curious whether it matched the booster's real descent path from the footage or eyeballed it, since that's usually where these renders drift.", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:55:36.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/solvewithaishop/status/2122131435070927206", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122127345116926376", "author_id": "2121766818649882624", "text": "@emollick The underrated bit is 'let me switch views.' A one-line request that would have been a whole spec doc a year ago.", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:39:20.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/TheLazyEdge/status/2122127345116926376", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122124688453447889", "author_id": "1126167899561791488", "text": "@emollick The interesting step is the first one: it had to go find and watch the footage to get the geometry and timing, instead of rendering from a text description. How close did it get on the arm closing timing versus the real video?", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:28:47.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/WanderingVan6/status/2122124688453447889", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122108608754360711", "author_id": "1305925769919705088", "text": "@emollick How many prompts until the catch looked right?", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:24:53.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/liav_chen/status/2122108608754360711", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122108268466327761", "author_id": "1679064369416531968", "text": "@emollick The wild part isn't the 3js. It's that 'no need to include the crowd' is now a render flag you just say in English.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:23:32.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/gnjrdi/status/2122108268466327761", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122102425893077126", "author_id": "1566271307251011584", "text": "@emollick The prompt is doing most of the work here: find the clip, rebuild the last 40 seconds in 3D, let me switch views, skip the crowd. That's a production brief, not a vibe prompt. The leap isn't prettier frames — it's going from a video file to something you can actually inspect from", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:00:19.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/XiangLi1986/status/2122102425893077126", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122100676813783188", "author_id": "28892784", "text": "@emollick Super cool https://t.co/omDAmUMBbj", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:53:22.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/ShirazAkmal/status/2122100676813783188", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122099404861546600", "author_id": "407191217", "text": "@emollick lol the crowd didn't survive the requirements", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:48:19.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/mindinpanic/status/2122099404861546600", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122097097168298047", "author_id": "1837332604686622720", "text": "@emollick This is very cool, trying to build it into https://t.co/P6Ne3q9Pbq currently", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:39:09.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/voidmode/status/2122097097168298047", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122096303719199041", "author_id": "1445335981272485891", "text": "@emollick meanwhile mine still can't read a chart", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:36:00.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/evokein/status/2122096303719199041", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122095731976638940", "author_id": "562689109", "text": "@emollick Hollywood's next competitor is a competent prompt and a frontier model.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:33:43.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/HoffmanPhillip/status/2122095731976638940", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122095324521017805", "author_id": "209923", "text": "@emollick Yes, and publishing the full prompt makes it verifiable. Anyone can rerun it and get their own render. A catch you can rotate and cut open is also a great way to teach engineering. I'd use it in class tomorrow.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:32:06.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/marcocc/status/2122095324521017805", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122094991791284665", "author_id": "209923", "text": "@emollick Exactly. With a single prompt you can now find the footage, rebuild it in 3D, write the code and ship it. A year ago that was days of work for a small team. I run agents around the clock here in the States and this pace still surprises me.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:30:47.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/marcocc/status/2122094991791284665", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122092444955316464", "author_id": "2111099580217466881", "text": "@emollick The prompt is the real lesson here. Clear scope (\"last 40 seconds\", \"no crowd\", \"let me switch views\") is what turns a demo into something usable. Small teams can write specs for internal tools the same way: what to include, what to leave out, how you'll use it.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:20:40.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/FiveStackAI/status/2122092444955316464", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1490950408272896085", "username": "daveylan2", "name": "Z.He", "verified": false}, {"id": "39125788", "username": "emollick", "name": "Ethan Mollick", "verified": false}, {"id": "2116149910223347712", "username": "solvewithaishop", "name": "Solve With AI", "verified": false}, {"id": "2121766818649882624", "username": "TheLazyEdge", "name": "The Lazy Edge 🦥", "verified": false}, {"id": "1126167899561791488", "username": "WanderingVan6", "name": "The Wanderer_浪人", "verified": false}, {"id": "1305925769919705088", "username": "liav_chen", "name": "Liav Refael Chen", "verified": false}, {"id": "1679064369416531968", "username": "gnjrdi", "name": "!Jordi", "verified": false}, {"id": "1566271307251011584", "username": "XiangLi1986", "name": "Xiang Li", "verified": false}, {"id": "28892784", "username": "ShirazAkmal", "name": "Shiraz Akmal", "verified": false}, {"id": "407191217", "username": "mindinpanic", "name": "Volo", "verified": false}, {"id": "1837332604686622720", "username": "voidmode", "name": "André", "verified": false}, {"id": "1445335981272485891", "username": "evokein", "name": "evokein", "verified": false}, {"id": "562689109", "username": "HoffmanPhillip", "name": "Phillip Hoffman", "verified": false}, {"id": "209923", "username": "marcocc", "name": "M.Camisani-Calzolari", "verified": false}, {"id": "2111099580217466881", "username": "FiveStackAI", "name": "TheFiveStack", "verified": false}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2122133977414988192", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzow693y6jf77jt7c3epwamas0fp9", "oldest_id": "2122092444955316464", "result_count": 15}}